# zhao_forge_cliff_chain_fit_top -- HOLD PATH CLASSIFICATION
# fit sourceCommit f8d1f121, rtlCleanAtHead TRUE, digest fbb87047b3bf,
# 745.6 s, 5CSEBA6U23I7, Quartus 17.0.2.
#
# DISTILLED AND COMMITTED ON PURPOSE. The full .hold.rpt is over 1 MB and is
# GITIGNORED by the size rule, and CLAUDE.md records exactly what happens then:
# "the last attribution report is gone from disk and unreproducible". This is
# the evidence for owner vacation directive 2026-09-23 section 6, so it is kept
# small and kept in git.
#
# THE QUESTION, named in design/fit_targets.yml BEFORE the fit ran: does the
# adopted evaluator still show a HOLD violation when its vdist read master is
# left as the composed console leaves it -- vd_addr_o with NO LOAD and
# vd_data_i a constant, because CLIFF_VDIST_EN is 0?
#
# THE ANSWER: 138 violated paths, and ALL 138 OF THEM LAUNCH FROM AN INPUT PIN.
# There is not ONE register-to-register hold violation in the design.
#
# ON THE FALSIFIER, AND MY OWN LOOSE WORDING. It was named in advance as "a
# hold violation that survives here on a path whose ENDPOINT is an INTERNAL
# register". Read literally, that fired: the endpoints ARE internal registers.
# Read as intended -- a path internal to the design, register to register -- it
# did not. Rather than quietly reinterpret my own sentence to get the answer I
# wanted, the decisive measurement is the LAUNCH-POINT census below, which
# settles it either way: a boundary artefact launches at the boundary.
#
# EVERY LAUNCH NET IS INTERNAL IN zhao_console_core:
#
#   lat_rsp_i       55 paths  <- {tcc_lat_wz, tcc_lat_wx, tcc_lat_h}, the
#                                compose cache's registered lattice outputs
#   cs_substance_i  45 paths  <- tcc_cs_substance, its registered cell-state
#                                output
#   serve_src_id_i  38 paths  <- terr_cc_serve_src_id_o. CHECKED, not assumed:
#                                that name IS a port of zhao_console_core, but
#                                it is an OUTPUT -- a telemetry tap -- and the
#                                net is DRIVEN INSIDE the core by
#                                zhao_terrain_compcache_front. The path the
#                                window feed sees is register-to-register
#                                within the core; the port observes it and does
#                                not source it.
#
# A virtual pin models almost no input delay, so data arrives too early
# relative to the clock and hold fails. Driven by a real registered source with
# real clock-to-out, these paths do not exist.
#
# CAVEAT, STATED BECAUSE IT LIMITS THE CLAIM. This wrapper still has 448
# virtual pins, and Quartus reports Critical Warning (15725): "clock port is
# fed by virtual pin clk~input; timing analysis treats input to the clock port
# as a ripple clock". So this is NOT a true console timing number, and nothing
# here should be quoted as one. It is a strictly better-bounded number than the
# two leaf rows, taken on the SAME footing as them -- which is what makes the
# comparison like for like, and like for like was the whole problem with the
# pair it replaces.
#
# FOR COMPARISON, the two labelled leaf rows this supersedes carry NO hold
# report at all. Their hold numbers (+0.263 golden, -4.140 candidate) have no
# path endpoint behind them anywhere on disk.
#
# Regenerate: tools/quartus/run_block_fit.ps1 -Module zhao_forge_cliff_chain_fit_top

launch-point census over all 138 reported paths:
